Data source attribution
=======================

This package contains no catalogue data. It contains a mapping: an ontology, a
SKOS scheme of nineteen department names, a connection descriptor, and two RML
TriplesMaps that describe how to read a database. Every title, artist name and
accession fact a consumer sees is fetched from that database at query time and
is never copied into this repository or into anything this repository
publishes.

The data those mappings read is the Metropolitan Museum of Art's Open Access
catalogue — the CSV export of the Met's collection records.

  Source:         The Metropolitan Museum of Art Open Access
                  https://github.com/metmuseum/openaccess
  Terms of use:   https://www.metmuseum.org/information/terms-and-conditions/open-access

The Met releases the Open Access catalogue data under CC0 1.0 Universal. That is
the Met's grant over their data, not ours, and it is reproduced here as
attribution rather than as a representation — a consumer relying on it should
read the Met's terms directly, since the Met may change them. The Met's grant
covers the catalogue metadata; it does not cover the images, which carry their
own terms, and this package maps no image.

"The Metropolitan Museum of Art" and "The Met" refer to the museum. This package
is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or produced in cooperation with the
Metropolitan Museum of Art.

The IRIs under https://data.metmuseum.org/ that this package mints are minted by
this package, in a namespace the Met controls, so that an object or a department
has one identity across every consumer that installs this. The Met does not
serve them and does not warrant them.

Everything in this repository that Semvia authored — the ontology, the
department scheme, the connection descriptor, the mapping documents, and this
notice — is dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal. See LICENSE.
